{"id": "EUVD-2026-86641", "enisaUuid": "4c5a1537-c8fc-39f4-a767-7f5993dae179", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvirtio_input: reset device if input_register_device() fails\n\nProbe marks the device DRIVER_OK with virtio_device_ready() before\ncalling input_register_device(). If registration fails, the error path\ncleared vi->ready and called del_vqs() while the device was still live,\nso the device could keep DMA to queues that were already torn down.\n\nMatch remove/freeze: call virtio_reset_device() on that path before\ntearing down the virtqueues.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:11:54", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/087b9ee4d36968329c846e6846e4e50f66532888", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16c90260ae7ae32d7ac9128fb5da404c37154765", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9a7e107734137f098f9b81e5615aa5a02c5395c7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8407da8974326c1ffdfe6a5a9bfc8fed3212bbdf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/668ebfea7ba623450b12fdeaa0d080464d0c0a14", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/81489b32a21c9360f8750d1fb600155d27452e19"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6x39-q2c6-8xg8", "CVE-2026-97987"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ea63528-640d-3026-84c4-a39768cc7aab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "271c865161c57cfabca45b93eaa712b19da365bc <668ebfea7ba623450b12fdeaa0d080464d0c0a14"}, {"id": "13850ade-b814-3928-a202-2f5a3a0f645a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "271c865161c57cfabca45b93eaa712b19da365bc <81489b32a21c9360f8750d1fb600155d27452e19"}, {"id": "2de1602e-6d1c-33e8-87ac-12a141ebb1ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "445a5def-b4b5-3c6b-aacb-63a648466413", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "271c865161c57cfabca45